---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import { Aside } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import BrickBoard from '../components/BrickBoard.astro';
import ledger from '../data/ledger.public.json';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url.ts';

const t = ledger.tests;
const fmt = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US');
const interpreters: string[] = ledger.determinism.interpreters;
const seeds: number[] = ledger.determinism.hash_seeds;
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Psyche status',
    description: 'The paused Psyche substrate: what is built, what is verified, and what was stopped.',
  }}
>
  <Aside type="caution" title="Paused">
    Psyche is paused while the thesis takes priority (decision D-031). No new work starts on it; its tests
    and checks stay maintained.
  </Aside>

  <p>
    Psyche is a dependency-free Python memory-and-activation substrate. What it shows is that its lower layers
    are correct and deterministic. It makes no claim that any layer reproduces a cognitive effect: three
    attempts to grade one were stopped before any graded run, each at a structurally distinct wall:
    semantic priming was circular, the fan effect found the mechanism absent, and interoception found the
    signal flat. The finding is scoped to this substrate and these three yardsticks.
  </p>
  <p>
    The captured test run has {t.suites} suites, {fmt.format(t.assertions)} assertions and {t.failures} failures,
    with identical counts on CPython {interpreters.join(', ')} and determinism probed under {seeds.length} hash seeds.
    The meaning bar is {String(ledger.meaning_bar.status).toLowerCase()}.
  </p>

  <section class="sx-section">
    <h2>Bricks</h2>
    <BrickBoard />
  </section>

  <p>
    Read more: <a href={withBase('psyche/overview/')}>What Psyche is</a>,
    <a href={withBase('psyche/architecture/')}>Architecture</a> and
    <a href={withBase('psyche/methodology/')}>Methodology</a>.
  </p>
</StarlightPage>
